{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And they shall make an ark</b> — The verse returns to the children of Israel mentioned above, and afterwards \"and you shall overlay it\" (Exodus 25:11), \"and you shall cast for it\" (Exodus 25:12) — all of them are in singular language, because Moses stands for all Israel (Mekhilta Yitro 1). And it is possible that it alludes to the fact that all Israel should participate in the making of the ark, because it is the holiest of the dwellings of the Most High, and so that they all may merit the Torah. And so they said in Midrash Rabbah (Exodus 34:2): Why is it that concerning all the vessels it is written \"and you shall make,\" but concerning the ark it is written \"and they shall make an ark\"? R. Yehudah son of R. Shalum said: The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Let everyone come and be occupied with the ark, so that they may merit the Torah. And the meaning of \"occupation\" is that each one should donate one gold vessel for the ark, or assist Bezalel with a little help, or that they should intend the matter:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:16:11.848311924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}